                <pb facs="0500" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg440"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Runyon</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-20"><hi rendition="#italic">August 20,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Department informed that the Prussian Government on 16th instant, in advance of
                    expected discussion, revoked concession Mutual Life Insurance Company, to take
                    effect September 1. If this report be correct, you are instructed strongly to
                    represent injustice of proceeding in view of our previous representations and of
                    the willingness of company to confine business in Prussia to plans approved by
                    the Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adee</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
